WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.900
From the myths of the Middle Ages, to fantasy
novels, to popular television shows with horrible

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.970
last seasons, there is one mystical creature
that has stood the test of time again and

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.970
again.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:17.690
For almost as long as human beings have gathered
together and shared stories, the imaginations

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.960
of countless generations have been captivated
by the same image.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.440
An enormous winged reptile, soaring through
the skies, sometimes depicted as a wise, noble

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.650
creature, and other times feared as it breathes
fire down upon its foes.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.630
For as long as there have been people to tell
them, there have always been tales of dragons,

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.120
be they benevolent or monstrous.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.420
But these are just stories, aren’t they?

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.620
But surely a legend does not survive for so
many centuries without a reason.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:52.079
And with all the other myths and ancient folklore
that the SCP Foundation has found to be true,

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:58.040
who’s to say that there aren’t still dragons
somewhere up in the mountains?

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.399
SCP-3844 was one such creature.

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:05.280
First discovered in 1906, a creature exactly
like the legends described was found to be

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.450
living in the Dolomites, a mountain range
located in north eastern Italy.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.810
One of the first to see it was a man named
Doctor Lester Fegmont, and he recounted his

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:20.200
findings to a friend, Frederick, in a letter
that the SCP Foundation keeps on file.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:26.009
This document is one of the first recorded
sightings of SCP-3844, and details how Lester

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:30.209
eventually came face to face with the winged
beast of legend.

00:01:30.209 --> 00:01:35.789
Having spotted something that they instantly
recognized as a dragon, Lester, his associate,

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:39.380
Galviston, and a guide traversed the slopes
of the Dolomite Mountains to find where the

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.500
creature had made its home.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.079
According to the description of the beast
in Lester’s letter, “It soared over one

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:50.319
peak, let out a low roar that loosened snow
from the mountainside, and then dived out

00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:51.319
of sight.

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:54.689
Its wings blocked out the sun like a cloud
passing overhead.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:57.719
I wish the whole lab could have seen it.”

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:01.179
After two hours, the group arrived at the
dragon’s cavern.

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:05.989
From the way Lester described it, the place
was like the lair of Smaug, the dragon famously

00:02:05.989 --> 00:02:07.460
featured in J.R.R.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.729
Tolkien’s The Hobbit.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.880
The cave was filled to the brim with treasure,
and seemed to stretch on deeper into the mountain

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.000
than the supplies they’d brought with them
would allow them to explore.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.160
But there was no sign of the creature they
had seen flying overhead.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.780
Giving up on their search, the group began
to leave the treasure-filled cave, preparing

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.750
to head back down out of the mountains the
way they had come.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.990
But then, they heard the roar.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.940
Still in the dragon’s lair, Lester had no
idea if the sound had come from in front or

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.360
behind, until they saw the creature outside
the cave’s entrance.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.010
Lester was terrified, but then he realized
something: the dragon wasn’t trying to threaten

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:51.380
the men, he was welcoming the intrepid trio
as its guests.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:56.470
SCP-3844 apparently spoke very eloquently
to the group, sounding like quite the gentleman

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.790
according to Lester.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:02.220
It seemed to possess some sort of shape shifting
ability, as the letter describes the creature

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.880
“changed its form to resemble a young man
to make us feel more relaxed.”

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.630
The dragon referred to the group as “a new
age of knights” and seemed to be very up

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.970
to speed on the current affairs of 1906.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:21.190
What followed was a lengthy negotiation between
Lester and SCP-3844, agreeing on terms that

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.520
would keep the dragon confined to the Dolomite
Mountain range and away from the prying eyes

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.740
of the public.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:32.200
It seemed that the group had been sent in
to deal with SCP-3844 on behalf of Italian

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.200
officials.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.620
In his letter, Lester mentioned his uncertainty
in placing his trust in the creature, hoping

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.020
not to be double crossed, and transcribed
the conditions that were agreed upon.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:47.590
The dragon, whose name was apparently Tharnock,
but was also referred to as ‘The Anomaly’,

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:52.180
was to limit the amount of times it ventured
out of its cave to only once per day, and

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.890
keep its flights within the area of the Dolomites.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:59.800
Tharnock was also advised to refrain from
roaring or vocalizing whenever it left its

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.800
lair.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.520
In return, Lester and his Anomaly Investigation
Foundation would send an ambassador to confer

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.890
with the dragon once a week, and punish anyone
who attempted to steal any valuable artefacts

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.930
from the creature’s hoard of treasure.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:18.209
Lastly, the Nation of Italy swore to encourage
its citizens to avoid traveling to the Dolomite

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:24.280
Mountains, and would publicly discredit any
eyewitness reports, denying Tharnock’s existence.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:29.789
Many years passed, and Doctor Lester Fegmont
rose through the ranks of the SCP Foundation,

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:35.930
eventually becoming known as O5-2, a member
of the infamous O5 Council.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:41.240
SCP-3844 was kept confined to the same area
within the Dolomites, but the methods of keeping

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.340
it there began to change.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.630
The Foundation set up a perimeter around the
area, keeping civilians from entry.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:52.319
They installed anti-aircraft artillery near
the cave where Tharnock was first found, to

00:04:52.319 --> 00:04:57.080
be used against the dragon in the event of
a full scale containment breach.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:01.879
Researchers were sent in to study the creature,
taking temperature and radiation readings,

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:07.779
testing SCP-3844’s IQ and providing it with
magazines on science, nature, and current

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:09.779
affairs as reading material.

00:05:09.779 --> 00:05:15.590
The Foundation learned that SCP-3844, much
like the dragons of legend, was able to breathe

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.590
fire.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.410
Or, more accurately, the beast could expel
a vapour of methane from its mouth, and then

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.939
ignite this gas via unknown means.

00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:28.789
Tharnock could speak at least seven languages,
and claimed it could mimic the form of any

00:05:28.789 --> 00:05:29.789
human.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:34.620
The contents of the dragon’s lair was estimated
to be worth almost 13.4 million United States

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:39.610
dollars, and it was learned that SCP-3844
would burrow underneath the treature when

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.610
it slept.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.350
If those traits sound familiar, that’s because
they are all recurring ideas that feature

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:49.169
in the various legends of dragons from throughout
the ages.

00:05:49.169 --> 00:05:54.779
In fact, SCP-3844 claimed to have been the
inspiration behind many European myths that

00:05:54.779 --> 00:05:56.909
revolved around dragons.

00:05:56.909 --> 00:06:02.319
It even asserted that it had been the model
for the Welsh flag, which depicts a red dragon

00:06:02.319 --> 00:06:03.469
in its center.

00:06:03.469 --> 00:06:10.749
From time to time, O5-2, would still visit
his old friend SCP-3844 for chats in the dragon’s

00:06:10.749 --> 00:06:11.749
cave.

00:06:11.749 --> 00:06:16.349
During one of their conversations, the dragon
and O5-2 discussed some of the many scientific

00:06:16.349 --> 00:06:21.669
advancements human beings had made over the
years, which SCP-3844 learned about through

00:06:21.669 --> 00:06:23.870
the reading material it had been provided.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.949
“How long had you known about the nature
of light?”

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:32.169
SCP-3844 asked, to which Doctor Fegmont replied
“Decades at least.”

00:06:32.169 --> 00:06:36.599
The dragon also asked about what it called
‘the inner workings of our smallest building

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:42.020
block’, and O5-2 explained that mankind
had split the atom during the second world

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.030
war.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:48.520
SCP-3844 then asked if science could explain
his kind, expressing a longing to stretch

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.199
his wings again and leave the confines of
his cave.

00:06:52.199 --> 00:06:57.099
O5-2 denied the dragon’s request, claiming
that advances in radar technology posed a

00:06:57.099 --> 00:07:01.710
potential risk to SCP-3844 if it was allowed
to take flight again.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:06.409
He offered to at least find a way to make
the dragon’s home bigger and more comfortable,

00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:08.660
before he bid the creature farewell.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.499
As they parted, both said that they hoped
to see each other again, which they would,

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.659
but only one final time.

00:07:15.659 --> 00:07:22.319
When they met for what would be the last time,
O5-2 returned to the cave at SCP-3844’s

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:23.319
request.

00:07:23.319 --> 00:07:28.159
The dragon was surprised to see that Lester
was still alive after so many years, and hadn’t

00:07:28.159 --> 00:07:31.669
succumbed to old age and death the way most
humans do.

00:07:31.669 --> 00:07:37.199
The doctor explained that as a member of the
O5 Council, he was kept in “pristine condition”

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:40.210
through thaumaturgy and temporal technology.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:45.059
The dragon described it as magic, and O5-2
argued that everything in the world can be

00:07:45.059 --> 00:07:48.839
explained with science if one examines for
long enough.

00:07:48.839 --> 00:07:53.169
SCP-3844 agreed, although appeared defeated
by this admission.

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:57.529
It asked Lester to explain what he thought
the stars to be, and the doctor naturally

00:07:57.529 --> 00:08:00.460
gave a scientific answer “Balls of flaming
gas.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:04.649
If you want me to be more specific, I could
list their chemical components.”

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:08.899
The dragon was already aware of this thanks
to its reading material, but then asked “Do

00:08:08.899 --> 00:08:13.729
you know what a duke once told me many, many
years ago when I asked him the same thing?

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:16.999
He said, ‘They're little lights from the
heavens.’

00:08:16.999 --> 00:08:21.720
His voice spoke with awe, much like yours
when we first met.”

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:26.369
At first, O5-2 thought the creature was grieving
over the advancements humanity had made in

00:08:26.369 --> 00:08:30.180
science, and how it had allowed them to better
understand the world.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:35.600
But SCP-3844 grieved for the death of spectacle,
the death of the belief in miracles.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:41.070
“I wish I could embrace science, but it
takes away so much of what I enjoy about this

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:46.490
world of ours,” the beast lamented, before
adding “It appears I'm allergic to the stuff.”

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:52.180
Learning about the world around it in such
detail had robbed SCP-3844 of its enjoyment

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.510
of the world.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:58.220
Knowing everything could be explained by and
reduced to science saddened the dragon, losing

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:02.060
the wonder that comes from not knowing all
the answers.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:06.550
With a heavy heart, the ancient creature proclaimed
it wanted to break the agreement it had made

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:09.450
with Doctor Fegmont all those years ago.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:14.800
O5-2 tried to argue with the beast, to convince
the dragon to stay in its lair, but Tharnock

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.550
had not felt the wind beneath his wings in
over a hundred years, and longed to be with

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.930
others of his kind.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:25.880
“You seem quite confident, '' O5-2 remarked
when the dragon announced its intention to

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.320
once again fly freely.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.920
“Confidence is all I have left.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:34.080
I don't want to believe that the world doesn't
need its whimsy anymore.”

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.660
Sadly, Tharnock’s flight was not to last.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:43.800
As dictated by the Foundation’s Special
Containment Procedures, SCP-3844 was neutralized,

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:47.800
shot down by the anti-aircraft guns that were
positioned around its cavern.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:54.240
The ancient, noble creature was no more, killed
for wanting to be free, for longing to believe

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.670
the world could still be a place filled with
wonder.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:02.271
Curiously, the remains of the dragon that
the SCP Foundation recovered seemed to, in

00:10:02.271 --> 00:10:08.070
actual fact, be those of a Draco Volans, a
non-anomalous species of lizard colloquially

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.400
known as the “Common Flying Dragon.”

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.990
These remains were kept under observation
by the Foundation’s research personnel,

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:20.250
and the cave where SCP-3844 had spent most
of its life was to be inspected every seventy

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:23.220
two hours for any signs of anomalous activity.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:28.440
But somehow, through means still inexplicable
to the Foundation, the entrance to the cave

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.560
seemed to disappear almost entirely.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:37.190
The area where SCP-3844 had been found and
was then kept prisoner no longer contained

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.190
a cavern.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:41.820
The lair filled with riches, gems and valuables
had vanished.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:45.500
In its place, was a small hole, and behind
it?

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.500
Dragons.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:52.200
Ever since the death of Tharnock, the designation
of SCP-3844 has been reassigned, to a collection

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:56.750
of large, winged reptiles that reside deep
within a number of mountains all over the

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.750
world.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:03.200
The SCP Foundation received multiple confirmed
reports of these creatures living in the Himalayas,

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:08.340
the Rockies, the Appalachians, the Andes and
the Dolomite Mountain ranges, where the very

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:15.440
first instance of SCP-3844 had been discovered,
all the way back in 1906.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.480
Being the most familiar with Tharnock, O5-2
was assigned to investigate the sudden appearance

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:24.320
of these creatures, and tasked with the challenge
of containing them.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:29.220
Tharnock had been slain, killed by the Foundation
for wanting nothing more than to be free in

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.470
a world of wonder and intrigue.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:36.110
However, one thing seemed clear, he was not
the only one of his kind.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:41.470
Rest assured and don’t mourn too much for
Tharnock, there are still dragons living in

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.500
the mountains.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:49.360
Now go check out “SCP-1762 - Where The Dragons
Went” and “SCP-348 - A Gift from Dad”

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.290
for more SCPs that’ll bring a tear to your
eye!

